lib/ — shared, version-pinned code that more than one step compiles in.

The versioning rule. A folder lib/<name>/vN/ is frozen once any step imports
it: from then on nothing in it is ever edited again. Before that, fixes are
allowed only if they keep every value identical (e.g. splitting an expression
for the compiler), and the module's tests must still pass. A change of any
kind after a step imports it, even a fix, makes lib/<name>/v(N+1)/ beside it,
and a step moves to the new version by changing its own Makefile. A step that
uses vN keeps building and drawing exactly what it did.

This bends the project's copy-don't-modify rule only as far as it must. Old
steps are untouched and keep their own copies; only a step that names a lib
version in its Makefile uses it. Each version carries its own tests and
mutants (make test, make mutants, make typecheck, with SDK= as in the steps).

lib/ant/v1/  The black garden ant, Lasius niger worker, from steps 44/55-57,
             posed by a simulation. First used by step 79.

Cross-machine renders (from step 79). A simulated world is recorded once and every
machine renders from the record; renders on different GPUs are near-identical, not
bit-identical (step 79: 1/255 almost everywhere, two refracting-crystal pixels at 8-10/255).
For a future film rendered on more than one machine, state this tolerance BEFORE the second
machine renders: per channel, the 99.9th percentile of |diff| <= 2/255, and the max
<= 16/255, reported with the count of pixels over 2/255. Step 79 keeps its own recorded test.
